{
  "id": "Compound::DB04843 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Mepenzolate, a cholinergic antagonist, is linked to Chrm1 through a series of molecular and functional interactions. The evidence suggests that Mepenzolate binds to Chrm2, which is a G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor, and that Chrm2 participates in G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity, which is associated with Chrm1. This implies a potential role for Mepenzolate in modulating Chrm1 activity through its interaction with Chrm2. The lowest common ancestor of Mepenzolate and Clidinium, an antimuscarinic agent, further supports the classification of Mepenzolate as an organic molecule with antimuscarinic properties, which may contribute to its interaction with Chrm1. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Mepenzolate could influence Chrm1 through its effects on G-protein coupled receptors, suggesting a broader role in neurotransmitter signaling.",
